e=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">10</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">1</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">20 </td>\r\n  <td>uninfecteds</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">67</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n\r\n</tbody></table><br><br>Where Run is used to organize the data.<br><br></div><div><br></div><div>I can get the data tidy based on Run if I don&#39;t include infection status or movement odds, but I just can&#39;t figure out how to get it to work when those two variables are included as rows. I&#39;m not sure if this will involve pure R trickery or if some of the reshaping should be done in Excel prior to reading it to R.</div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be appreciated- if someone needs an actual Excel file to goof around with rather than the abbreviated table I provided, just let me know.</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>Michael Culshaw-Maurer</div></div>"
