   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hey Jaime and Matt,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve attached a sample of my data in a CSV file. The issue I&#39;m having is that the output places some variables in rows, but then the actual observations (counts at each time step) are in rows as well. If I remove the MovementOdds and InfectionStatus rows, then I can get it in R as a data.frame and then use tidyr::gather to get it how I need it, but then I&#39;m stuck without InfectionStatus and MovementOdds. If I read it into R with those two rows included, the formatting gets all screwy because R wants to read everything with the variables in columns.</div><div><br></div><div>Hopefully the sample data will make it easier to see what I&#39;m working with. Thanks!!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Tuesday, July 26, 2016 at 1:56:35 PM UTC-7, Jaime Ashander wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Michael, <div><br></div><div>To do it quickly you might break the data.frame into two and reshape them separately.</div><div><br></div><div>For a better solution, it would be easier for me (probably others too) if you provided your data (just a sample) in a format easily inputtable into R. You could do the following, assuming you already have your data in a data.frame in R that is named dat:</div><div><br></div><div>dput(head(dat))</div><div><br></div><div>and then paste the results into the email.</div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Jul 26, 2016 at 1:51 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">mjculsh...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve currently got an output from NetLogo in a CSV file, but the formatting of the data is a bit strange. I need some help getting it into a usable format in R, but I can&#39;t quite figure out how to get it there. I&#39;ve gotten partway using tidyr::gather, but I need a bit more help.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s the output I get: </div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"562\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:562pt\">\r\n\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"107\" style=\"width:107pt\">\r\n <col width=\"65\" span=\"7\" style=\"width:65pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"15\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"15\" width=\"107\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:107pt\">Run</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">1</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" width=\"65\" style=\"width:65pt\">1</