   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: Tidying some weirdly formatted data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hey guys,<div><br></div><div>Just figured it out- I needed to transpose my data, and then tidyr::gather worked like a charm.</div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s the breakdown of what I did:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Enter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> code here</span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#000\">d </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font></div></code><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dt &lt;- t(d)</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">colnames(dt) &lt;- dt[1,]</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dt &lt;- dt[-1,]</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dt &lt;- as.data.frame(dt)</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">setDT(dt, keep.rownames = T)[]</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">colnames(dt)[1] &lt;- &quot;Run&quot;</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">colnames(dt)[4:53] &lt;- c(seq(1,50,1))</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dtg &lt;- gather(dt, Time, Count, 4:53)</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dtg$Run &lt;- gsub(&quot;\\\\.[0-9]*$&quot;, &quot;&quot;, dtg$Run)</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dtg &lt;- arrange(dtg, Run, InfectionStatus, Time)</font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#666600\" face=\"monospace\">dtg</font></div></div><br>I&#39;m sure there&#39;s likely a more elegant way to go about doing this, but it seemed to work fine, and I&#39;ve got the data organized just how it should be.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Michael</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
